diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b677f4e..4075d0f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,4 +6,27 @@ A small expense ledger. Entries live in a JSON file (`--data` or `$LEDGER_DATA`)
     python -m ledger list
     python -m ledger report --by month
 
-Tests: `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.
+For a monthly recurring expense, supply both recurrence options:
+
+    python -m ledger add 2026-01-31 25.00 subscriptions "monthly plan" --repeat monthly --until 2026-03-31
+
+This series produces entries on January 31, February 28, and March 31. Each
+month uses the original day, clamped to that month's last day (February 29 in a
+leap year). The end date is inclusive: ending the example on March 30 would
+include only January and February. Ending on the start date produces one entry.
+Listing and both reports include all occurrences, including future ones, with
+the original amount, category, and note. Negative amounts represent refunds.
+
+Only `monthly` is supported. `--repeat monthly` requires a valid `--until` date
+in `YYYY-MM-DD` form on or after the start date; `--until` requires `--repeat`.
+Invalid recurrence options exit with status 2 and a message on stderr, without
+creating or changing the data file.
+
+The JSON file stores one object per ordinary entry or recurring series, never
+one row per occurrence. Series add `"repeat": "monthly"` and `"until"` fields to
+the usual entry fields. Existing JSON-list files, including entries without a
+note, remain readable and accept both ordinary and recurring additions.
+Use the global `--data PATH` option before the command to choose a file, or set
+`LEDGER_DATA`; the default is `ledger.json`.
+
+Tests: `python -B -m unittest discover -s tests`.
